0..61 Comment "//! No case tells the two orders of a commutative meet apart."
62..65 Comment "//!"
66..142 Comment "//! The apartness of two terms gives a value of the type with no value. So a"
143..218 Comment "//! wrong apartness makes each statement provable. The two orders of a meet"
219..294 Comment "//! are one term, and a rule that tears under the symmetry decides nothing."
295..298 Comment "//!"
299..375 Comment "//! The check of a block reads each rule in each order of the arguments of a"
376..455 Comment "//! meet. It refuses a block where the two orders of one rule give two results."
456..459 Comment "//!"
460..536 Comment "//! The checker compares two terms in each order of the arguments of a meet."
537..615 Comment "//! It refuses a case with no arm where one order joins the two terms. A block"
616..690 Comment "//! whose rules do not join gives no type of terms, so a case over them is"
691..731 Comment "//! refused by the refusal of the block."
732..735 Comment "//!"
736..752 Comment "//! - see: #8323"
754..777 Comment "// `Hollow` and `Pick`."
